# Agent Skills (ULG ecosystem)

Skills are registered as `agent_skill:<slug>` entities and delivered by **canonical slug** (`Use the <slug>` skill — seat self-fetches). Check before manually re-deriving an ingestion procedure or tool pattern the team has encountered before.

**Invariant**: ∀ non-standard document type or tool pattern (financial statements, legal filings, insurance docs, frontier dispatch, browser sessions, …): Use the relevant skill by slug before attempting the operation; ¬ re-derive what is already documented. ¬ `fs`-read skill markdown into context.

**In-session discovery (all seats):** discovery is **native** — description-gated
rule stubs attach (plugin `*_ulg.mdc` + checkout-local `*_ws.mdc`); the native
`<available_skills>` index surfaces census skills from the `ulg-ecosystem` plugin
and checkout-local `.cursor/skills/*/SKILL.md` stubs whose `description` matches
the task; web seats use boot manifest + description triggers. Read the matched
stub; it defers to the skill SOT via seat self-fetch on explicit use.

Index / discovery (fallback — metadata only, not body load):
```
cortex(tool="entities", arguments='{"type": "agent_skill"}')
cortex(tool="entity_get", arguments='{"entity_id": "agent_skill:<slug>"}')
```
